Not a solution but I was able to make a workaround (with a "unique" function at least) by casting the Null type columns to String or something else (looking forward to a better fix):
```
import polars as pl
df = pl.DataFrame(
    {
        "integer": [],
        "date": [],
        "float": [],
        "string": [],
    },
).lazy()
print(
    df.select(
        [
            pl.col(field_name).cast(pl.String)
            if isinstance(field_dtype, pl.Null)
            else pl.col(field_name)
            for field_name, field_dtype in df.schema.items()
        ]
    )
    .unique()
    .fetch()
)
```
